# Layered architecture

| Layer | Owns | Must not |
|---|---|---|
| `api/http` | DTO → command, one prebound call, presenter, status mapping | import `domains/*` except via `composition`, import `infra` or Drizzle |
| `composition` | adapters (translation only) and wiring (prebound scenarios) | business rules, Express |
| `domains/<name>` | scenarios `(cmd, deps)`, policy, entity, private repository | other domains, `api`, Express, `new Date()`, `randomUUID()` |
| `queries` | SELECT for one screen, flat DTO | writes, domain imports |
| `infra` | pool, schema, unit of work, jwt, passwords, outbound HTTP | domains, `api`, composition |
| `core`, `shared`, `config` | primitives, business values, env | domains, `api`, `infra` (config and core), anything but `core` (shared) |

- A domain `*.repository.ts` and its `*.module.ts` may import `infra/db`. Nothing else in the domain may. The repository is not exported from `index.ts`.
- Outside a domain, import `domains/<name>/index.ts` only.
- Two domains meet only in `composition/adapters`. Wiring prebinds deps; controllers do not assemble them.
- Repositories take no `tx` argument. `infra/db/unit-of-work.ts` stores the client in `AsyncLocalStorage`. The scenario that owns the process calls `deps.tx.transaction()`; a nested call joins it.
- Lists and reports go through `queries/`, not through a domain entity.
- `npm run lint` runs dependency-cruiser. Never relax a forbidden rule to make a change pass.
- `src/main.ts` opens the pool. `src/app.ts` does not import a domain or the database. `src/server.ts` is the only listener.

Procedure: `express-resource` skill. Audit: `architecture-audit` skill.
